Any person who carries on banking business in Nigeria without a valid licence commits an offence and is liable on conviction to:
(a) imprisonment for a term of not less than five years;
(b) a fine of not less than N50,000,000;
(c) two times the cumulative deposits or other amount collected; or
(d) both imprisonment and fine [1].

